⸻

Project Goal

Implement a fully functional web-based Education Management System with 3 clearly defined user groups:
	•	Regular User (Student)
	•	Content User (Course Manager)
	•	Administrator (System Admin)

⸻

Activity Flow (Detailed Rules)

A. Regular User (Student)

Viewing Courses
	•	User visits the website.
	•	User selects menu “Course List”.
	•	System displays all available courses.
	•	User selects a course to view details (curriculum, schedule, instructors).

Course Registration
	•	User selects a course from the list.
	•	Clicks “Register for Course”.
	•	System checks login state:
	•	If not logged in: Redirect to login page.
	•	If logged in: Confirms registration and returns success/failure notification.

Doing Exercises
	•	User logs in.
	•	Visits “My Courses”.
	•	Chooses a registered course.
	•	Selects “Exercise List”.
	•	Completes an exercise and clicks “Submit”.
	•	System saves submission and updates status.

User Login
	•	User clicks “Login”.
	•	Inputs email and password.
	•	System authenticates:
	•	Success: Redirects to user home.
	•	Failure: Returns error message.

Group Chat
	•	User logs in.
	•	Visits “Group Chat”.
	•	Selects or creates a chat group.
	•	Sends and receives messages in real-time.

⸻

B. Content User (Course Manager)

Create/Delete Courses
	•	Logs into the system.
	•	Navigates to “Course Management”.
	•	Creating a course:
	•	Selects “Add New Course”.
	•	Inputs details (name, description, duration).
	•	Saves course data.
	•	Deleting a course:
	•	Selects course and confirms deletion.
	•	System removes course from database.

Creating Content and Exercises
	•	Selects managed course.
	•	Chooses “Add Content and Exercises”.
	•	Inputs lesson content, exercises, and deadlines.
	•	Saves information to database.

Creating/Deleting Chat Groups
	•	Navigates to “Chat Group Management”.
	•	Creating a group:
	•	Selects “Create New Chat Group”.
	•	Inputs name, description, and adds members.
	•	Deleting a group:
	•	Selects a group, confirms deletion, and removes it from database.

User Approval
	•	Visits “User Approval” section.
	•	Sees a list of pending user registrations.
	•	Approves or rejects user registrations.
	•	Updates user status accordingly.

Posting Lectures
	•	Selects managed course.
	•	Chooses “Post Lecture”.
	•	Uploads lecture files (PDFs, videos, articles).
	•	Confirms and saves to database.

Adding Users
	•	Navigates to “User Management”.
	•	Selects “Add New User”.
	•	Inputs user details (name, email, role).
	•	Confirms and creates user account.

⸻

C. Admin User (System Administrator)

Managing Users
	•	Logs into admin dashboard.
	•	Selects “User Management”.
	•	Views the full list of users.
	•	Performs CRUD actions (Create, Read, Update, Delete) on user data.
	•	Saves changes to the database.

User Statistics & Reports
	•	Selects “User Statistics”.
	•	Views user activity data and statistics in visual charts.
	•	Exports statistics as Excel/PDF reports.

⸻

Database Schema (Detailed ERD Rules)

Entities:

User
	•	id (PK), name, email (unique), password_hash, role (USER, CONTENT_USER, ADMIN), created_at, updated_at

Course
	•	id (PK), name, description, duration, content_user_id (FK User.id), created_at, updated_at

CourseRegistration
	•	id (PK), user_id (FK User.id), course_id (FK Course.id), registered_at

Lecture
	•	id (PK), course_id (FK Course.id), title, description, file_url, uploaded_at

Exercise
	•	id (PK), course_id (FK Course.id), title, content, deadline, created_at

ExerciseSubmission
	•	id (PK), exercise_id (FK Exercise.id), user_id (FK User.id), submission_content, submitted_at, score, graded_at

ChatGroup
	•	id (PK), name, description, created_by (FK User.id), created_at

ChatGroupMember
	•	id (PK), group_id (FK ChatGroup.id), user_id (FK User.id), joined_at

Message
	•	id (PK), group_id (FK ChatGroup.id), sender_id (FK User.id), content, sent_at

UserApproval
	•	id (PK), user_id (FK User.id), content_user_id (FK User.id - reviewer), status (PENDING, APPROVED, REJECTED), reviewed_at

AdminReport
	•	id (PK), generated_by_admin_id (FK User.id), report_type (USER_STATS, COURSE_STATS, ACTIVITY_STATS), file_url, generated_at

⸻

ERD Relationships:
	•	User (1-n) Course: managed by Content User.
	•	User (n-n) Course: via CourseRegistration.
	•	Course (1-n) Lecture.
	•	Course (1-n) Exercise.
	•	Exercise (1-n) ExerciseSubmission.
	•	User (1-n) ExerciseSubmission.
	•	ChatGroup (1-n) ChatGroupMember.
	•	User (n-n) ChatGroup: via ChatGroupMember.
	•	ChatGroup (1-n) Message.
	•	User (1-n) Message.
	•	User (1-n) UserApproval: Reviewer (Content User).
	•	User (1-n) UserApproval: Reviewed User.
	•	User/Admin (1-n) AdminReport.

