AI Development Rules & Recommendations
	•	Structure & Clarity:
Clearly separate each user group’s logic into Laravel Controllers and routes.
	•	Follow Laravel Best Practices:
Use Eloquent ORM, resource controllers, and resourceful routing.
	•	Authentication & Middleware:
Implement Laravel’s built-in authentication (auth) and custom middleware for role-based access (User, Content User, Admin).
	•	Error Handling & Notifications:
Standardize responses using Laravel responses (JSON API or standard Blade views). Clearly handle errors and provide user-friendly feedback.
	•	Use of Laravel Relationships:
Properly define and leverage Eloquent Relationships (hasOne, hasMany, belongsTo, belongsToMany).
	•	Database Migrations & Seeders:
AI must generate comprehensive migrations for all tables and relationships. Use seeders for default roles, test users, and sample courses.
	•	Blade Templates & Frontend:
Clearly structured UI components using Blade for views. AJAX or Livewire recommended for dynamic content updates (chat/messages/submissions).
	•	Testing:
AI should include PHPUnit test-cases for controllers and models.
	•	Security:
Apply Laravel security best practices (validation, sanitization, CSRF protection, password hashing).

